  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 233 PM CDT Sat Aug 22 2026\n\nCurrent surface analysis places broad high centered over \nsouthern Manitoba into the eastern Dakotas, while a low is \nstarting to develop to the lee of the Rockies. Upper level \nanalysis places high over New Mexico, with ridge running \nnorthward generally to the lee of the Rockies. Over our area, \nlight winds remain over most locations, though are becoming \nsoutheasterly and increasing over our southwest in response to \nthe developing low.\n\nFor tonight, surface high pushes east with south-southeasterly\nwinds on the increase, particularly over western areas.\n\nOn Sunday, south-southeasterly winds will continue over the area\nresulting in increasing low-level moisture and higher humidity\nvalues. Of note will be increasing instability values over\nsouthwestern into south central North Dakota, with some guidance\nnoting CAPE values exceeding 2000 J/Kg, though guidance is\nkeeping deep layer shear marginal and also possibly capped \ngiven the possible limited heating due to mid-level cloud cover.\nTherefore, will keep severe threat marginal at this point \nfocused mainly over the southwest/south central.\n\nAs we get into Monday night, the next thunderstorm threat pushes\nin from Montana late as another short wave makes its approach,\nagain posing a marginal severe threat. Chances then spread east\nthrough the day on Monday as the wave and surface trough/front\nslide easterly. Again, guidance is suggesting elevated\ninstability as we get into primarily central/eastern North\nDakota with marginal shear, but then timing of this system comes\ninto play. Therefore, will continue to focus on the marginal\nthreat. \n\nOn Tuesday, western ridge remains in place but a very compact\nshort wave/low slides down the face of the ridge, but at this\npoint only looks to graze our northeastern areas. Therefore,\nmost locations are expected to remain mild and dry, though some\nprecipitation chances will be in place mainly around the Turtle\nMountains.\n\nRidge to the west slowly creeps east and remains the dominating\nfactor keeping temperatures near to above average through the\nremainder of the forecast, though a few waves pushing through do\nbring occasional precipitation chances.",
